NOTE
Captions for shop-tour.mp4.
This clip has no dialogue, so every cue below is a non-speech sound. Captions are
NOT just a transcript of speech: WCAG 1.2.2 requires captions to include any sound
that carries meaning. A deaf viewer who is given only dialogue captions still misses
the doorbell, the counter bell and the telephone - which is the whole soundtrack here.

Conventions used:
  - non-speech sound goes in square brackets
  - a speaker's name would be written as "NAME: dialogue"
  - cues stay on screen long enough to read: roughly 20 characters per second

